// Dataset recording: the record button on a commander with a recorder slot
// (the web panel or XR headset), which the family's control wires, and the
// episode recording a model starts on the stack's MCP endpoint, where the
// recorder is listed as its robot's whatever the commander. The family's
// control supplies the ordered limb observations and actions and the
// dataset rate, and the robot's fragment robot_type and storage_root.
//
// storage_root is bind-mounted into the recorder container; /tmp lasts until
// reboot, so select durable storage for saved datasets. Setting s3_uri
// (s3://bucket/prefix, including R2) mirrors saved episodes to the bucket.
// The recorder reads AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
// AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3, and AWS_DEFAULT_REGION from the launch environment.
{
  peppy_schema: "launcher_fragment/v1",

  deployments: [
    {
      source: { name: "lerobot_recorder", tag: "v1" },
      instances: [{ instance_id: "recorder_inst" }],
    },
  ],

  adjustments: [
    // Skipped where the launch runs no MCP endpoint.
    { target: "robot_control_inst", add_links: { recorder: ["recorder_inst"] } },
  ],
}
